module match_applied_sum.neg_1

// A `match` on an `Option` that leaves `None` uncovered -- refused, as on any
// sum, and refused HERE rather than at the C compiler or at run time.
//
// Why the cell exists: the coverage rule asked only whether the scrutinee was
// a plain sum, and an applied one returned before any judgment. That was
// harmless while every `match` on an applied sum was refused at its head; the
// day `Option` and `Result` passed, this exact program was ACCEPTED by the
// first build of the wave, while the oracle says E_MATCH_NON_EXHAUSTIVE -- a
// silent acceptance of a program whose `None` would have read the result
// temporary's zero. The pair: pos_1.nv covers every variant and passes.

// NOVAC_EXPECT leaves a variant uncovered

fn first(o Option[int]) -> int => match o {
    Some(v) => v
}

fn main() {
    println(first(Some(1)))
}
